     4  Hypothesis (from experiment_005):
     5    The timeit-measured per-call time follows the model:
     6      measured_time(N) = true_time + overhead/N
     7    where overhead is the fixed timeit overhead per repeat. By measuring at
     8    multiple N values and fitting this model, we can estimate the true time
     9    (overhead→0) and the overhead itself.
    10  
    11    This is a linear model in 1/N:
    12      measured_time = true_time + overhead × (1/N)
    13  
    14    We fit this model to experiment_005 data and extrapolate to N=∞ (1/N=0)
    15    to get corrected times. We then compare corrected times with experiment_001
    16    (perf_counter) measurements.
    17  
    18  Design:
    19  - Uses experiment_005 data (already collected)
    20  - Fits linear model: time = a + b*(1/N) via least squares
    21  - Extrapolates to N=∞ for corrected times
    22  - Compares corrected times with experiment_001 perf_counter results
    23  - Validates model by checking R² and residual patterns
    24  - Python standard library only
