     5  
     6  ## Hypothesis
     7  
     8  From experiment_002 follow-up:
     9  
    10  The large gap between insertion sort and builtin_sorted at n=4096 suggests
    11  insertion sort becomes impractical well before that size. We should find the
    12  crossover point where insertion sort's total time exceeds builtin_sorted by a
    13  factor of 10 or more.
    14  
    15  **Expected ordering** (from lowest to highest crossover size):
    16  1. **sorted**: lowest crossover (O(n) best case)
    17  2. **random**: medium crossover
    18  3. **duplicates**: medium crossover (many equal elements reduce comparisons)
    19  4. **reverse**: highest crossover (O(n²) worst case)
    20  
    21  ## Design
    22  
    23  - **Sizes**: 8, 16, 32, 64, 128, 256, 512, 1024 (factor-2 steps)
    24  - **Input types**: random, sorted, reverse, duplicates (all four)
    25  - **Repetitions**: 100 per condition
    26  - **Seeds**: random=42, sorted=1, reverse=1, duplicates=99 (same as experiment_001)
    27  - **Correctness**: Verified on every measured input before timing
    28  - **Randomization**: Measurement order randomized (seed 12345)
    29  - **Timer**: time.perf_counter()
    30  - **Copying**: NOT timed — copy happens before timing starts
    31  
    32  ## Platform
    33  
    34  - Python 3.13.15, CPython
    35  - Linux-7.0.14-linuxkit-aarch64-with-glibc2.41
    36  - aarch64 architecture
    37  
    38  ## Results
    39  
    40  ### Summary Statistics (microseconds)
    41  
    42  | Size | Input    | Builtin (μs) | Insert (μs) | Ratio | Crossover? |
    43  |------|----------|-------------|-------------|-------|------------|
    44  | 8    | random   | 0.19        | 1.17        | 6.23x | No         |
    45  | 8    | sorted   | 0.16        | 0.49        | 3.02x | No         |
    46  | 8    | reverse  | 0.18        | 1.47        | 8.27x | No         |
    47  | 8    | duplicates| 0.23       | 1.08        | 4.77x | No         |
    48  | 16   | random   | 0.24        | 2.92        | 12.2x | **Yes**    |
